@startuml
title AISafe - Peer-to-peer GET Forwarding and Aggregation\n(aircraft-service example; same mechanism in every service)

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Client" as Client
participant "aircraft-1\n:8081" as A
database "H2\naircraft1" as StoreA
participant "aircraft-2\n:8082" as B
database "H2\naircraft2" as StoreB

== 1. Single resource ==

Client -> A : GET /api/hangar/aircraft/CS-TUA\nAuthorization: Bearer <JWT>
activate A
A -> A : validate JWT + role (ATCC / BACKOFFICE / ADMIN)
A -> StoreA : findById("CS-TUA")
StoreA --> A : empty

alt aircraft-2 answers
  A -> B : GET /api/hangar/aircraft/CS-TUA\nAuthorization: Bearer <JWT>\nX-Service-Key: <key>\nX-Forwarded-By: aircraft-1
  activate B
  note right of B
    Request has X-Forwarded-By:
    answer from local store only,
    never forward again (max 1 hop,
    no circular forwarding).
  end note
  B -> StoreB : findById("CS-TUA")
  alt Found on aircraft-2
    StoreB --> B : Aircraft
    B --> A : 200 OK + AircraftResponse
    A --> Client : 200 OK + AircraftResponse
  else Not found on aircraft-2
    StoreB --> B : empty
    B --> A : 404 Not Found
    A --> Client : 404 Not Found\n(not found on any replica)
  end
  deactivate B
else aircraft-2 unreachable: connection refused or no answer in 2 s
  note over A : if aircraft-2 is already marked as down,\nthe next two calls are skipped (fail fast)
  A -> B : GET ... (attempt 1)
  A -> A : wait 200 ms (backoff)
  A -> B : GET ... (attempt 2)
  A -> A : mark aircraft-2 as down for 10 s\n(circuit breaker) + log WARN
  A --> Client : 404 Not Found\nX-Partial-Result: true\n(not found on reachable replicas)
end
deactivate A

== 2. Collection query (aggregation) ==

Client -> A : GET /api/hangar/aircraft?status=AVAILABLE
activate A
par
  A -> StoreA : findByStatus(AVAILABLE)
  StoreA --> A : local list
else
  A -> B : GET /api/hangar/aircraft?status=AVAILABLE\nX-Forwarded-By: aircraft-1, X-Service-Key
  B -> StoreB : findByStatus(AVAILABLE)
  StoreB --> B : peer list
  B --> A : 200 OK + list
end
A -> A : merge lists, remove duplicates\nby registrationNumber, sort, paginate
A --> Client : 200 OK + aggregated list\n(X-Partial-Result: true if a peer failed)
deactivate A

legend bottom left
  Rules (implemented once in the forwarding component, reused by every service):
  - Local store first; peers only when the resource is missing locally (single GET)
    or always in parallel for collection queries.
  - X-Forwarded-By marks an internal request: it is answered locally and never re-forwarded.
  - Forwarded requests keep the user's JWT and add X-Service-Key; requests carrying
    X-Forwarded-By without a valid service key are rejected with 403.
  - Timeouts: connect 1 s, read 2 s; 2 attempts with 200 ms backoff; failed peer skipped for 10 s.
  - 404 only after every reachable replica answered "not found"; partial answers are flagged
    with X-Partial-Result: true and logged. Availability is preferred (AP, CAP theorem).
  - Commands (PATCH/PUT/DELETE) on a single resource follow the same lookup: the replica that
    does not hold the resource forwards the command to the peer that holds it.
endlegend
@enduml
